1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:01,200
t.

2
00:00:01,200 --> 00:00:03,435
One last door

3
00:00:01,200 --> 00:00:03,435
for my one last flyer.

4
00:00:03,435 --> 00:00:05,671
Aah!

5
00:00:03,435 --> 00:00:05,671
What are you doing here?

6
00:00:05,671 --> 00:00:07,240
Oh, uh,
just walking.

7
00:00:07,240 --> 00:00:08,708
Just walking
these dogs.

8
00:00:08,708 --> 00:00:11,177
[ Chuckles nervously ]
For their health.

9
00:00:11,177 --> 00:00:14,414
Mm-hmm.

10
00:00:11,177 --> 00:00:14,414
[ Chicken clucks ]

11
00:00:15,882 --> 00:00:18,417
Did you guys hear that?
Someone clucked.

12
00:00:18,417 --> 00:00:19,786
It wasn't you, right?

13
00:00:19,786 --> 00:00:20,920
[ Slurps ]

14
00:00:20,920 --> 00:00:22,622
Then it's got to be
that lost chicken.

15
00:00:22,622 --> 00:00:24,390
[ Groans ]
Come on, pups.

16
00:00:24,390 --> 00:00:26,926
I think this calls
for a rescue mission.

17
00:00:26,926 --> 00:00:28,428
Let's roll out.

18
00:00:29,895 --> 00:00:33,400
[ Grunting ]

19
00:00:36,569 --> 00:00:38,771
Come here. Ah.
Come here, buddy.

20
00:00:38,771 --> 00:00:40,807
Man:
For millennia, we've been taught

21
00:00:40,807 --> 00:00:42,475
that time is a constant stream,

22
00:00:42,475 --> 00:00:45,577
that traversing is impossible,
but who writes the textbooks?

23
00:00:45,577 --> 00:00:47,547
That's right. The government.

24
00:00:47,547 --> 00:00:50,550
They're keeping time travel
for themselves.

25
00:00:50,550 --> 00:00:53,119
But no longer.
I believe I've cracked the code.

26
00:00:53,119 --> 00:00:55,154
I've worked out the bugs
from my previous iterations,

27
00:00:55,154 --> 00:00:56,589
and not only that,

28
00:00:56,589 --> 00:01:00,993
I have procured
a new willing test subject.

29
00:01:00,993 --> 00:01:01,061
[ Gasps ] Mark.

